{"raw": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205217761442_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Coordinator of Nursing Simulation and Resource Center", "description": "Posted: 2026-08-21\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University has an opening for a Coordinator of Nursing Simulation and Resource Center. The Coordinator of Nursing Simulation and Resource Center is responsible for the organization and maintenance of a simulated nursing laboratory for students to practice and acquire the theoretical basis for psychomotor skills used in nursing. \u00a0Supervises various activities associated with the simulation lab. QUALIFICATIONS Candidates must have a strong personal Christian commitment and faith in Jesus Christ and a desire to serve others Must be committed to the mission of Huntington University as a comprehensive Christian College dedicated to educating men and women to impact our world for Christ Must have a minimum of two years in the practice setting Demonstrated understanding of Christian higher education Bachelor\u2019s degree in nursing required, Master\u2019s preferred Holds a valid, unencumbered nursing license in Indiana. Positive interpersonal skills and a team player Strong communications skills Demonstrated administrative and supervisory skills Commitment to continuous process improvement General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a full-time, exempt position. To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205184046552_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Academic Fieldwork Coordinator & Occupational Therapy Faculty", "description": "Posted: 2026-04-07\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nHuntington University has an opening for an Academic Fieldwork Coordinator and Assistant Professor of Occupational Therapy for the Doctoral Program at the Peoria, Arizona location. Faculty members of the occupational therapy program provide structured learning and laboratory experiences for students in compliance with ACOTE 2023 Standards. Faculty aligns teaching with university and department mission statements, strategic plan, curricular philosophy, design, and level of expertise. Faculty administer evaluations of the students, supports learning with application in areas of fieldwork, research, and experiential component. Faculty provide ongoing program evaluation and professional development for continued success of the academic program. The Academic Fieldwork Coordinator (AFWC) searches and secures memorandum of understanding (MOU) contracts for fieldwork I and II placements for individual doctor of occupational therapy students. The AFWC is responsible for accreditation standards, administrative management of (MOU) contracts, site evaluations, student on-site requirements, accreditation compliance, program evaluation, and other administrative duties as deemed necessary. QUALIFICATIONS Full-time faculty with an earned occupational therapy entry level degree and earned doctorate awarded by an institution that is accredited by a USDE-recognized regional accreditation body or via ACOTE external review from institutions outside of the United States Current occupational therapist license in Arizona Minimum of 2 years of clinical experience as an occupational therapist Strong personal Christian commitment and faith in Jesus Christ Commitment to stewardship of University resource and strong desire to serve others Able to work in a fast-paced, multi-task environment Excellent verbal and interpersonal skills Proficient in oral, written, and computer communications High level of computer literacy required Training and knowledge of office procedures, computer hardware and software (Microsoft Office) High level of organizational ability and attention to detail for electronic and paper documentation Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously Ability to track and maintain large volume of dated memorandums of understanding Commitment to confidentiality Maintain AOTA Code of Ethics Willingness to learn new computerized system management databases Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, students, the University community and clinical agencies Competent in research and database searches Flexibility to attend occasional after-hours program and university events General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a full time, 12-month faculty, exempt position. To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201102285674_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Game Development Adjunct", "description": "Posted: 2025-07-21\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nThe department of Digital Media Arts at Huntington University is seeking an online Game Development Adjunct Faculty member to develop two courses over the Summer of 2025\u00a0and then teach one course in the fall and one course in the spring of 2026. Develop curriculum and teach the following courses: - DM371 Game Development Studio I - DM381 Game Development Studio II Minimum Requirements: Bachelor's degree and five years of relevant work experience in Game Development Experience with video\u00a0game\u00a0engines such as Unity, Unreal,\u00a0Gamemaker, etc. and asset integration. Must have a strong personal Christian commitment and faith in Jesus Christ and a desire to serve others. Must be committed to the mission of Huntington University as a comprehensive Christian College dedicated to educating men and women to impact our world for Christ. Develop the curriculum for the courses GD371 and GD381 for the\u00a0Game\u00a0Development\u00a0major during the summer of 2025. Compensation is\u00a0$4,000. Expected to teach GD371 and GD381 during the 2025-2026 year. Instruction may be done remotely however\u00a0expected 1 in-person visit each semester with compensated travel pay. Compensation is\u00a0$6,000 for\u00a0both semesters. In total, the position will receive $10,000. Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a part-time position. \u00a0Teaching is on a semester-by-semester basis as University needs arise. General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a part-time, exempt adjunct position. \u00a0 To Apply: \u00a0 Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and include/upload a cover letter, Curriculum Vitae should include name, email address, postal address, phone number, all academic degrees earned with institutions, years attended, conferral dates, and discipline indicated. \u00a0 Also, include employment since college with dates of service and other relevant experience and names, email and postal address and phone numbers of two professional references. \u00a0\u00a0 Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201099030019_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Theatre Arts - Adjunct Faculty", "description": "Posted: 2025-07-09\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University is seeking adjunct faculty members for a variety of courses in bachelor\u2019s degree programs in Theatre, Theatre Performance, and Theatre Technology. Successful applicants will have a strong personal faith in Jesus Christ and an understanding of the integration of faith and art. Prior teaching and practical experience in the arts is essential.\u00a0This position requires teaching during fall or spring terms during daytime hours (no evening courses available).\u00a0Opportunities may also arise for directing or designing for productions as a guest artist. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS MFA, related Master\u2019s degree or Ph.D. degree preferred; minimum of a bachelor\u2019s degree in theatre, directing, performing arts, technical theatre, or related field required Teaching experience and demonstrated potential for college-level teaching Supportive of a Christian faith environment and the University\u2019s educational goals\u00a0 Should enjoy creatively and interactively teaching non-theatre majors Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a part-time position. \u00a0Teaching is on a semester-by-semester basis as University needs arise. General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a part-time, exempt adjunct position. \u00a0 To Apply: \u00a0 Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and include/upload a cover letter, Curriculum Vitae should include name, email address, postal address, phone number, all academic degrees earned with institutions, years attended, conferral dates, and discipline indicated. \u00a0 Also, include employment since college with dates of service and other relevant experience and names, email and postal address and phone numbers of two professional references. \u00a0\u00a0 Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200961478348_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "ADJUNCT Faculty - Clinical Mental Health Counseling", "description": "Posted: 2024-05-20\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nThe Clinical and Mental Health Counseling department has an opening for an adjunct instructor. \u00a0Under the direction of the Program Director, the instructor provides instruction for classroom and/or laboratory settings in coordination with the established course and program objectives.\u00a0 \u00a0QUALIFICATIONS Must\u00a0have\u00a0a\u00a0personal\u00a0relationship\u00a0with\u00a0Jesus\u00a0Christ,\u00a0a\u00a0strong\u00a0desire\u00a0to serve\u00a0others,\u00a0and\u00a0a\u00a0commitment\u00a0to being a\u00a0faithful steward of\u00a0University\u00a0resources Commitment towards the integration of Christian faith in teaching and practice Experience\u00a0and\u00a0understanding\u00a0of\u00a0Christian\u00a0higher\u00a0education Successful\u00a0experience\u00a0in teaching\u00a0at\u00a0the\u00a0university\u00a0level Participate\u00a0and\u00a0identify\u00a0with\u00a0the\u00a0counseling\u00a0profession\u00a0through\u00a0sustained\u00a0memberships\u00a0in\u00a0professional\u00a0counseling organizations. Maintain\u00a0certifications\u00a0and/or\u00a0licenses\u00a0related\u00a0to\u00a0the\u00a0counseling\u00a0profession\u00a0and\u00a0specialty\u00a0area(s); candidates should be fully licensed Strong clinical supervision preparation and ability Show evidence of sustained professional development and renewal activities related to\u00a0counseling; professional service and advocacy in counseling; research and scholarly activity in\u00a0counseling\u00a0commensurate\u00a0with their\u00a0faculty role. Education, Experience and Licensure: Required Education: Master\u2019s degree in counseling or related field Preferred Education: Master\u2019s degree in clinical mental health counseling, or in the process of earning a PhD in Counselor Education & Supervision. Ideally the candidate has an earned doctorate (Ph.D. in Counselor Education from a CACREP accredited program) Required Experience: \u00a0At least 5 years of teaching experience in course being taught and/or at least 5 years of specialized experience in the counseling or related field Required Licensure: For faculty supervisors teaching practicum/internship courses, candidates must be fully licensed in the counseling field for a minimum of 2 years (LMHC, LCPC, LPC, etc.) Preferred Licensure: Candidates should be fully licensed in the counseling field for a minimum of 2 years (LMHC, LCPC, LPC, etc.) Candidates will be reviewed based on their qualifications for specific courses that they will teach. \u00a0SPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES Teach course assignments depending on departmental needs and the candidate\u2019s education and experience Attend monthly department meetings and other meetings as needed Collaborate with course coordinator(s) and program directors as it relates to the teaching of the course(s) assigned General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a part-time, exempt adjunct position. \u00a0 To Apply: \u00a0 Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and include/upload a cover letter, Curriculum Vitae should include name, email address, postal address, phone number, all academic degrees earned with institutions, years attended, conferral dates, and discipline indicated. \u00a0 Also, include employment since college with dates of service and other relevant experience and names, email and postal address and phone numbers of two professional references. \u00a0\u00a0 Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200469304758_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "COMPLETE BY INVITATION ONLY - Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Posted: 2023-08-01\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nMISSION STATEMENT The University\u2019s mission is to develop a commitment to scholarship; educate, equip, and help students develop their abilities for a life of God-honoring service to others; and for personal fulfillment. \u00a0 BASIC FUNCTION: \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Under the direction of the Department/Division Chair, the instructor provides instruction for classroom and/or laboratory settings in coordination with the established course and program objectives.\u00a0 QUALIFICATIONS Must have a strong personal Christian commitment and faith in Jesus Christ and a desire to serve others Must be committed to the mission of Huntington University as a comprehensive Christian College dedicated to educating men and women to impact our world for Christ Demonstrated understanding of Christian higher education, preferred Demonstrated potential for college-level teaching Master\u2019s degree in related field or 5 years relevant experience Licenses and certifications-depending on area of instruction Additional qualifications as recommended for area of instruction Positive interpersonal skills and a team player Excellent communications skills Demonstrated administrative and supervisory skills Commitment to continuous process improvement \u00a0 SPECIFIC RESPONSIBILITIES Teach course assignments depending on departmental needs and candidate\u2019s education and experience Attend department meetings, when possible (no other faculty meeting/committee requirements) Total time commitment is less than 10 hours per week General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule: All adjunct positions are part-time, exempt positions. \u00a0Please indicate on application what position you were asked to apply for. To Apply: \u00a0 Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and include/upload a cover letter, Curriculum Vitae should include name, email address, postal address, phone number, all academic degrees earned with institutions, years attended, conferral dates, and discipline indicated. \u00a0 Also, include employment since college with dates of service and other relevant experience and names, email and postal address and phone numbers of two professional references. \u00a0\u00a0 Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director Human Resources. Curriculum Vitae. The CV should include name, email address, postal address, phone number, all academic degrees earned with institution, years attended, conferral dates, and discipline indicated.\u00a0 Employment since college with dates of service, and other relevant experience.\u00a0 Names, email and postal addresses, and phone numbers of two professional references.\u00a0 \u00a0 Note: \u00a0Official transcripts of all institutions attended will be required upon hiring.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200510627670_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "ASSISTANT COACH", "description": "Posted: 2023-04-03\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nNormal 0 false false false EN-US X-NONE X-NONE st1\\:*{behavior:url(#ieooui) } /* Style Definitions */ table.MsoNormalTable\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0{mso-style-name:\"Table Normal\";\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0mso-tstyle-rowband-size:0;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0mso-tstyle-colband-size:0;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0mso-style-noshow:yes;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0mso-style-priority:99;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0mso-style-parent:\"\";\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0mso-padding-alt:0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0mso-para-margin:0in;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0mso-pagination:widow-orphan;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0font-size:10.0pt;\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0font-family:\"Times New Roman\",serif;} MISSION STATEMENT : The University\u2019s mission is to develop a commitment to scholarship; educate, equip, and help students develop their abilities for a life of God-honoring service to others; and for personal fulfillment. BASIC FUNCTION : This is a part-time position. \u00a0Responsibilities include any tasks assigned by the head coach related to all facets of the sport such as recruiting, administration, practice assistance, scheduling, etc. and complying with all NAIA, Crossroads League, and institutional regulations and policies. QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates must have a strong personal faith in Jesus Christ and a desire to serve others Commitment to the mission and goals of Huntington University as a Christ-centered liberal arts institution Previous coaching experience is desired, but not required Commitment to an NAIA program of intercollegiate athletics Evidence of communication, managerial, organizational and coaching skills RESPONSIBILITIES: 1. \u00a0 \u00a0 Perform tasks as assigned by the Head Coach including, but not limited to \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 a. \u00a0 \u00a0 Recruiting \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 b. \u00a0 \u00a0 Administrative tasks \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 c.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0\u00a0 Practice Assistance \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 d.\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Scheduling \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 e. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Arranging travel accommodations \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 f. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 Spiritual development 2. \u00a0 \u00a0 Comply with all NAIA, Crossroads League and institutional policies", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200261222336_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Theatre Arts- Adjunct Instructor", "description": "Posted: 2022-02-21\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University is seeking adjunct faculty members for a variety of courses in bachelor\u2019s degree programs in Theatre, Theatre Performance, and Theatre Technology. Successful applicants will have a strong personal faith in Jesus Christ and an understanding of the integration of faith and art. Prior teaching and practical experience in the arts is essential. This position requires teaching during fall or spring terms during daytime hours (no evening courses available). Opportunities may also arise for directing or designing for productions as a guest artist. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS MFA, related Master\u2019s degree or Ph.D. degree preferred; minimum of a bachelor\u2019s degree in theatre, directing, performing arts, technical theatre, or related field required Teaching experience and demonstrated potential for college-level teaching Supportive of a Christian faith environment and the University\u2019s educational goals\u00a0 Should enjoy creatively and interactively teaching non-theatre majors General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a part-time position. \u00a0Teaching is on a semester-by-semester basis as University needs arise. To Apply: Apply via ADP and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200256424822_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor-Chemistry", "description": "Posted: 2022-02-08\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nAdjunct Instructor \u2013 Liberal Arts Chemistry Lab Huntington University seeks to fill an adjunct teaching position in chemistry.\u00a0 The qualified candidate will be asked to teach two or three sections of CH111L, Lab for Chemistry in Contemporary Society, per semester. Each lab section meets for one 2-hour time block per week. Evening hours are available if needed.\u00a0 \u00a0 Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in a chemistry or biology-related field, or 5 years of relevant laboratory experience Demonstrated potential for college-level teaching\u00a0 Familiarity with lab safety protocol and lab teaching logistics Supportive of a Christian faith environment and the University\u2019s educational goals\u00a0 Should enjoy creatively and interactively teaching non-science majors General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a part-time, exempt position.\u00a0 To Apply: \u00a0 Apply via ADP and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Jean Cole, Human Resources Manager.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200254409679_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Bus Driver", "description": "Posted: 2022-02-02\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University seeks part-time bus drivers for a 35 passenger bus.\u00a0 The Bus Driver is responsible for transporting students, staff, coaches, and passengers safely to and from their destination in the established times and in all types of weather and road conditions, observing legal, safe, and defensive driving practices. \u00a0QUALIFICATIONS: \u00a0 Must have a strong personal faith in Jesus Christ, a desire to serve others and a commitment to being a faithful steward of university resources Must have a \u201cclean\u201d driving record Have sufficient physical and mental abilities to operate a school bus/van in a safe manner Must be narcotic drug and alcohol free Professional driving experience preferred This is a part-time, on call position Must possess a valid commercial driver\u2019s with passenger endorsement Minimum age of 25 years\u00a0 RESPONSIBILITIES: \u00a0 Bus/Van Maintain vehicle by conducting safety inspection, inspect the interior and exterior and the engine prior to use Maintain order among passengers and report any behavioral issues to the appropriate personnel, assure passengers understand bus rules of safety Assist students, staff, coaches, and passengers in and out of vehicle as needed Assist students, staff, coaches, and passengers with loading and unloading equipment as needed \u00a0 Administrative \u00a0 Collaborate with coaching and administrative staff to establish transportation schedule Maintain and update route sheets and schedules, manifesto along with emergency contact information Assist with other projects and perform other duties as assigned by the VP of Business & Finance Treasurer\u00a0 Physical Requirements of the Position: \u00a0 Employee is regularly required to focus, see, speak, and hear and to have dexterity of the hands and fingers Must be able to sit for extended periods of time while driving Other duties may require bending, kneeling, twisting, and reaching overhead, above shoulders and horizontally May be required to lift, carry, and/or push moderately heavy persons in effort to evacuate the bus/van in case of emergency Shall be required to meet all regulatory standards as directed by the State of Indiana as a driver General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a part-time, non-exempt position. \u00a0The driving schedule varies depending on scheduling and workflow demands. To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205222645102_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "OTA Lab and Administrative Coordinator", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-10\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University has an opening for a OTA Lab and Administrative Coordinator. The OTA Lab and Administrative Coordinator supports the daily operation of the Occupational Therapy Assistant program by maintaining the OTA classroom and laboratory environments and providing administrative support to faculty, students, and program leadership. QUALIFICATIONS Strong personal faith in Jesus Christ and an understanding of the relationship between faith and professional practice. Occupational Therapy Assistant (OTA) certification preferred. Candidates with relevant patient care experience in a health-related field, such as experience as a Certified Nursing Assistant (CNA), Patient Care Technician (PCT), rehabilitation aide, or similar role, will also be considered. Commitment to supporting an occupational therapy practice curriculum grounded in the mission of the University and reflective of Christian ethics, compassion, and service. Strong organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills, with the ability to work collaboratively with faculty, students, the University community, and clinical partners. Proficiency with computer applications and technology needed to support departmental operations. Demonstrated commitment to stewardship and service to others. Commitment to maintaining confidentiality and handling sensitive information with professionalism and discretion. Self-directed, innovative, and able to assess current operations, identify areas for improvement, and develop practical strategies to enhance departmental functioning. \u00a0 General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts University. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a part time, non-exempt, 9-month position, working 20 hours per week.\u00a0 To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205230681607_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Coach Track & Field- Throws", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University has an opening for an Assistant Coach for Track & Field-Throws. The Track & Field Assistant Coach for Throws is a part-time position that supports the overall mission of the Track & Field program by providing expert technical instruction and mentorship to student-athletes in the throwing events. Grounded in Christ-centered values and a commitment to the University's mission, this role helps foster a caring, faith-driven environment where athletes are developed spiritually, personally, and competitively. \u00a0Responsibilities include coaching, recruiting, and administrative tasks as assigned by the head coach ensuring all operations reflect compliance with NAIA, conference, and institutional regulations.\u00a0 QUALIFICATIONS Christ-centered Faithfulness: A deep personal commitment to Jesus Christ and a passion for the mission of Huntington University, dedicated to mentoring student-athletes to impact the world for Christ. Commitment to Excellence: Proven skills in coaching, administration, and leadership Creativity and Innovation:\u00a0 Demonstration of forward-thinking approaches to skill development, team-building, problem-solving, and continuous process improvement. Collaborative Spirit: Evidence of ability to effectively communicate and collaborate with Athletic department personnel and to achieve shared team, department, and institutional goals. Community Conviction: Exceptional interpersonal skills, with the ability to build a supportive and growth-oriented culture for student-athletes and staff. GENERAL RESPONSIBILITIES: Coaching Serve as a consistent Christian role model, intentionally developing and mentoring student-athletes to grow in their faith and to impact our world for Christ. Plan and organize practices for the jumps events to maximize student-athlete potential and program performance. Recruiting Aid head coach in identifying and recruiting student-athletes who align with the HU mission, prioritizing those who are a strong fit for the university's spiritual, academic, and athletic standards. Develop an understanding of NAIA recruiting policies in order to maintain a high level of integrity throughout the recruiting process. Administrative Duties Maintain high standards of excellence and timeliness in completing administrative tasks assigned by the head coach. Proactively anticipate program needs to enhance the student-athlete experience and work with the head coach to create a plan to meet the needs. Collaboration & Supervision Foster a collaborative spirit by working closely with the head coach and other coaching staff to ensure effective program operations. Communicate and enforce team rules that promote a culture of accountability and care. Comply with all NAIA, Crossroads League, and institutional policies. General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a part-time position. \u00a0 To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205230679911_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Coach Track & Field - Jumps", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University has an opening for an Assistant Coach for Track & Field-Jumps The Track & Field Assistant Coach for Jumps is a part-time position that supports the overall mission of the Track & Field program by providing expert technical instruction and mentorship to student-athletes in the jumping events. Grounded in Christ-centered values and a commitment to the University's mission, this role helps foster a caring, faith-driven environment where athletes are developed spiritually, personally, and competitively. \u00a0Responsibilities include coaching, recruiting, and administrative tasks as assigned by the head coach ensuring all operations reflect compliance with NAIA, conference, and institutional regulations.\u00a0 QUALIFICATIONS Christ-centered Faithfulness: A deep personal commitment to Jesus Christ and a passion for the mission of Huntington University, dedicated to mentoring student-athletes to impact the world for Christ. Commitment to Excellence: Proven skills in coaching, administration, and leadership Creativity and Innovation:\u00a0 Demonstration of forward-thinking approaches to skill development, team-building, problem-solving, and continuous process improvement. Collaborative Spirit: Evidence of ability to effectively communicate and collaborate with Athletic department personnel and to achieve shared team, department, and institutional goals. Community Conviction: Exceptional interpersonal skills, with the ability to build a supportive and growth-oriented culture for student-athletes and staff. GENERAL RESPONSIBILITIES: Coaching Serve as a consistent Christian role model, intentionally developing and mentoring student-athletes to grow in their faith and to impact our world for Christ. Plan and organize practices for the jumps events to maximize student-athlete potential and program performance. Recruiting Aid head coach in identifying and recruiting student-athletes who align with the HU mission, prioritizing those who are a strong fit for the university's spiritual, academic, and athletic standards. Develop an understanding of NAIA recruiting policies in order to maintain a high level of integrity throughout the recruiting process. Administrative Duties Maintain high standards of excellence and timeliness in completing administrative tasks assigned by the head coach. Proactively anticipate program needs to enhance the student-athlete experience and work with the head coach to create a plan to meet the needs. Collaboration & Supervision Foster a collaborative spirit by working closely with the head coach and other coaching staff to ensure effective program operations. Communicate and enforce team rules that promote a culture of accountability and care. Comply with all NAIA, Crossroads League, and institutional policies. General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a part-time position. \u00a0 To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205199783540_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Agricultural Education", "description": "Posted: 2026-06-10\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University has an opening for a tenure track faculty position, Assistant Professor of Agricultural Education. \u00a0Primary responsibilities include leading and recruiting for Huntington University's agricultural teacher education program. This position reports to the Director of Haupert Institute for Agricultural Studies and works in close collaboration with the Director of Teacher Education and the Managing Director of the Haupert Institute for recruiting activities and events.\u00a0 QUALIFICATIONS Must have a strong personal Christian commitment and faith in Jesus Christ and a desire to serve others Must be committed to the mission of Huntington University as a comprehensive Christian College dedicated to educating men and women to impact our world for Christ Demonstrated understanding of Christian higher education and commitment to Christian faith integration in teaching and mentorship Master's degree in Education or Ag Education; or a B.S. with considerable experience in the same; must hold a current teaching licensure for teaching agriculture at the secondary education level Experience teaching agriculture at the high school or middle school level Demonstrated success with engagement in Ag Education and the broader agricultural community Past history of service in FFA or 4-H; experience in agriculture judging events or team management preferred Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Able to work collaboratively with others in a variety of settings Current membership and/or willingness to join professional organizations such as the Indiana Association for Agricultural Educators (IAAE), the National Association of Agricultural Educators (NAAE), the American Association for Agricultural Education (AAAE), or the North American Colleges and Teachers of Agriculture (NACTA) Candidates will be given preferential consideration if they have experience and/or credentials in CTE core pathway topics, including but not limited to: animal, plant, or agribusiness systems, ag leadership and communications, environmental and natural resources, food products and processing, or power and structure systems (ie: ag mechanics, welding, construction, etc.). General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule:\u00a0 This is a full time, 10-month faculty, exempt position. To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205231153975_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Film Production & Capstone Director", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University has an opening for an Assistant Professor of Film Production & Capstone Director. Under the direction of the Dean of the Arts, the Assistant Professor of Film Production will teach and mentor students within a hands-on, project-based curriculum while continuing professional work that contributes to the growth of the Film & TV Production program. The position will also serve as Director of the Capstone Film Program, leading students in significant feature-length cinematic productions that emphasize intentional storytelling and professional production practices. The focus is on nurturing students\u2019 artistic expression and helping them channel their God-given talents toward successful careers in film. This is an 11-month, tenure-track faculty position. QUALIFICATIONS Strong personal Christian commitment and faith in Jesus Christ and a desire to serve others. Commitment to the mission of Huntington University as a comprehensive Christian university dedicated to educating men and women to impact our world for Christ. Demonstrated understanding of Christian higher education preferred. 5 years of professional film production experience strongly encouraged. Teaching experience in film production, screenwriting, or related areas preferred. Professional experience in areas such as directing, producing, cinematography, post-production, sound, production design, or screenwriting is highly valued. Terminal degree (MFA or Ph.D.) preferred. Strong interpersonal, communication, and organizational skills. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with faculty, students, and industry professionals. Energetic, student-centered teacher and mentor who enjoys working alongside students in production environments. Commitment to continuous improvement, creative innovation, and professional excellence. General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Schedule: This is a full-time, 11-month tenure track exempt faculty position. For more information, please see https://www.huntington.edu/digital-media-arts To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205233696554_4&lang=en_US": {"title": "Visiting Instructor, Core Liberal Arts & Sciences", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-24\n\nLocation: Huntington\n\nHuntington University has an opening for a full-time Visiting Instructor to teach broadly across our Core4 interdisciplinary curriculum and Forester Foundations general education courses. This is a three-year, grant-funded teaching position running from January 2027 through December 2029. Teaching and meeting with students are the heart of this position. However, this role also requires a successful candidate to be involved in the life of the mind across campus, engaging with both Academic Affairs and Student Life. The position carries no committee assignments and no advising responsibilities within a major, so the person who takes it can give full attention to the classroom and on-campus student experience. Mission Alignment Huntington University's Forester Foundations curriculum asks every core course to help students analyze their subject matter from a Christian perspective. A faculty generalist in this role brings that same faith integration to whatever discipline they're teaching that semester, whether it's a Core4 course built around belonging, creativity, discovery, or flourishing, or a general education course. QUALIFICATIONS Must have a strong personal Christian commitment and faith in Jesus Christ and a desire to serve others. Must be committed to the mission of Huntington University as a comprehensive Christian College dedicated to educating men and women to impact our world for Christ. Demonstrated understanding of Christian higher education and commitment to faith integration in teaching. Master's degree required; earned doctorate (Ph.D.) preferred. Demonstrated excellence in undergraduate teaching, ideally including experience in general education, interdisciplinary, or first-year seminar contexts. Comfort and versatility teaching across disciplines, since this role moves between Core4 and general education coursework rather than staying within a single department. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a genuine interest in mentoring students outside of the classroom. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty and staff across multiple departments and programs. Work Schedule: This is a full-time, 9-month tenure track exempt faculty position.\u00a0 General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith To Apply: Review the full job description attached for a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications. Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and upload a cover letter, resume and list of references with your completed application. Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.", "department": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205174755563_1&lang=en_US": {"title": "Adjunct Professor of Psychology- AZ Location", "description": "Posted: 2026-03-03\n\nLocation: Peoria\n\nHuntington University Arizona is seeking an adjunct faculty member to teach PY111 Introduction to Psychology for the spring semester. PY111 is a 3-credit undergraduate course designed to introduce students to the scientific study of behavior and mental processes. This course surveys major principles, methods, and findings in psychology, including development, learning and memory, biological bases of behavior, cognition, social and personality psychology, motivation and emotion, mental health, and ethical practice. Students are also introduced to psychological research methods and the application of psychology through a Christian worldview COURSE OVERVIEW PY111 emphasizes: Foundational psychological concepts and terminology Scientific reasoning and interpretation of psychological research Active student engagement through discussions, applied activities, and research labs Integration of psychology with ethical practice and a Christian worldview Instruction includes lectures, discussion, quizzes, research lab activities, and a comprehensive final exam, with readings delivered through Perusall and Moodle MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS : Master\u2019s degree in psychology or a closely related field (or equivalent professional experience) Teaching experience or demonstrated potential for effective college-level instruction Supportive of a Christian faith environment and the mission of Huntington University Enjoys engaging students through interactive and discussion-based teaching \u00a0 THE ADJUNCT PROFESSOR WILL BE RESPONSIBLE FOR: Teaching PY111 in accordance with the university catalog, course syllabus, and departmental guidelines Preparing course materials, assessments, and grading student work in a timely manner Providing a course syllabus to students and the division office as requested Maintaining accurate student records and required academic documentation \u00a0Communicating promptly and professionally with students, faculty, and staff Supporting student engagement, ethical academic practices, and inclusive classroom learning Performing other related duties as assigned General Information: \u00a0 Huntington University is an independent, Christian liberal arts university. \u00a0Employees of Huntington University subscribe to the Statement of Faith that is identical to that of the National Association of Evangelicals. \u00a0 Statement of Faith Work Sch edule:\u00a0 This course meets once per week. To Apply: \u00a0 Apply via ADP, using your personal email, and include/upload a cover letter, Curriculum Vitae should include name, email address, postal address, phone number, all academic degrees earned with institutions, years attended, conferral dates, and discipline indicated. \u00a0 Also, include employment since college with dates of service and other relevant experience and names, email and postal address and phone numbers of two professional references. \u00a0\u00a0 Questions can be emailed to Andy McKee, Director of Human Resources.", "department": ""}}, "rows": {"https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205217761442_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 430, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205217761442_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Coordinator of Nursing Simulation and Resource Center", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-08-21", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205184046552_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 430, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205184046552_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Academic Fieldwork Coordinator & Occupational Therapy Faculty", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Academic Fieldwork Coordinator & Occupational Therapy", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2026-04-07", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201102285674_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 430, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201102285674_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Game Development Adjunct", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "department of Digital Media Arts", "area_key_words": "spring of", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2025-07-21", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201099030019_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 430, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201099030019_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "Theatre Arts - Adjunct Faculty", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "Supportive of a Christian faith", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2025-07-09", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200961478348_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 430, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200961478348_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "ADJUNCT Faculty - Clinical Mental Health Counseling", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "ADJUNCT; Christian liberal arts university", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2024-05-20", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200469304758_1&lang=en_US": {"school_id": 430, "posting_url": "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=7353b4b0-47be-41c8-bcb3-dc2ae3843581&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9200469304758_1&lang=en_US", "job_title_in_post": "COMPLETE BY INVITATION ONLY - Adjunct Instructor", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "2023-08-01", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mas